### What is the maximum path sum problem?

Given a binary tree where each node has an integer value (which may be negative), find the maximum sum over any connected path. A path is a sequence of nodes where each pair of adjacent nodes is connected by an edge. The path can start and end at any node and does not need to pass through the root.

```java
package com.bank.model;

public class ProfitNode {
    public String centerId;
    public int profit; // can be negative (loss)
    public ProfitNode left;
    public ProfitNode right;

    public ProfitNode(String centerId, int profit) {
        this.centerId = centerId;
        this.profit = profit;
    }
}
```

### How do the two quantities work?

The key insight is keeping two quantities separate. The upward gain is what a node can contribute to its parent: the node's value plus the better of its two children's gains. The bending path is the full path that turns at this node: the node's value plus both children's gains. The return value feeds upward; the global captures the bend.

```java
package com.bank.service;

import com.bank.model.ProfitNode;

public class MaxPathSum {
    private int maxSum = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

    public int maxPathSum(ProfitNode root) {
        maxSum = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        gain(root);
        return maxSum;
    }

    private int gain(ProfitNode node) {
        if (node == null) return 0;

        int leftGain = Math.max(gain(node.left), 0);   // clamp negative to 0
        int rightGain = Math.max(gain(node.right), 0);  // clamp negative to 0

        // Bending path through this node (both branches)
        int bendingPath = node.profit + leftGain + rightGain;
        maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, bendingPath);

        // Upward gain: can only extend through one child
        return node.profit + Math.max(leftGain, rightGain);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        //       Finance(10)
        //       /          \
        //    Ops(20)      Risk(-5)
        //   /     \          \
        // HR(7)  IT(15)    Audit(3)
        ProfitNode finance = new ProfitNode("Finance", 10);
        ProfitNode ops = new ProfitNode("Ops", 20);
        ProfitNode risk = new ProfitNode("Risk", -5);
        ProfitNode hr = new ProfitNode("HR", 7);
        ProfitNode it = new ProfitNode("IT", 15);
        ProfitNode audit = new ProfitNode("Audit", 3);

        finance.left = ops; finance.right = risk;
        ops.left = hr; ops.right = it;
        risk.right = audit;

        MaxPathSum solver = new MaxPathSum();
        System.out.println("Max path sum: " + solver.maxPathSum(finance));
    }
}
```

